 "_": "THE APPROVED APPEARANCE, AS DATABASE ROWS. Each case is exactly what the Spine stores — an exam_stimuli kind and spec, plus the exam_questions.reading that selects the variant — and nothing else. Both sides of the visual suite render it through renderForQuestion(), the one entry point content goes through, so the specimen and the exam cannot disagree about how a row becomes a figure; the only thing that differs between them is the page around it, which is what is being tested. scripts/check-visual-fidelity.cjs compares the pixels against the committed baselines in tests/visual-baselines/. Changing a case changes the contract, and the new baseline has to be looked at by a person before it is committed. geo-2 exists because niceStep crosses from a one-unit step to a two-unit step the moment a window passes nine units across, and the two windows the grammar page happened to show both sit under it — so the squared-paper family shipped ruled every TWO units, uncountable, with every check green. A contract only covers the failures it has a case for. pie-0 carries TWO panels because a pie stimulus routinely does — one population cut two ways — and a single-panel contract would not have caught a second panel drawn on top of the first. pie-1 is one panel with a 5% slice, which is where a rim label stops fitting beside its own wedge.",
