   "_why": "TWO SERIES ON A BAR CHART. The suite had one-series bars only, and the configuration it was missing is the one that broke: a direct label centred over its own bar ran straight through the taller sibling bar beside it. The LAST group here is deliberately the shape that collided -- the labelled series shorter, a taller sibling next to it -- so this baseline fails if a label ever moves back over a bar. The data is invented for this sheet and belongs to no form; every value sits on a ruled line, which is what a reading='value' chart must be."
